Project Title: EduStream Digital Learning System. 
Technology Stack: ASP.NET Web Forms, C#, SQL Server, HTML5, CSS3, JavaScript.

1. Multimedia & HTML5 Elements (Layout):
The master page uses <header>, <nav>, <main>, and <footer> tags. We integrated a video simulation for 'Virtual Lab' using the HTML5 <video> tag and an interactive 'Learning Object' using <canvas> for a quiz visualization. Inline CSS is used for the urgent 'System Alerts' banner, Internal CSS for page-specific layout overrides in the 'Course Catalog', and a robust External Stylesheet for the global grid system.

2. User Authentication & Member/Admin Modules:
The system features a Registration.aspx page with ASP.NET Validation controls (RequiredFieldValidator and RegularExpressionValidator for email formats). Members access a dashboard to view resources. Admins have an 'Admin Dashboard' to manage content. 
Code Snippet (Authentication): 
protected void btnLogin_Click(object sender, EventArgs e) {
    string query = "SELECT Role FROM Users WHERE Username=@U AND Password=@P";
    SqlCommand cmd = new SqlCommand(query, conn);
    cmd.Parameters.AddWithValue("@U", txtUser.Text);
    cmd.Parameters.AddWithValue("@P", HashFunc(txtPass.Text));
    // ... execute and set Session["UserRole"] ...
}

3. CRUD Operations & Database Connectivity:
The Admin module allows full resource management. 
- Insert: Add new PDF/Video resources via FileUpload.
- Display: GridView with paging for resource listings.
- Update: Edit resource descriptions/titles via SQL Update command.
- Delete: RowDeleting event in GridView removes records from the 'Resources' table.
All database connections use a centralized connection string in Web.config for security and maintainability. Form validation prevents SQL injection by utilizing parameterized queries throughout the application.
